# Interactive User Registration Foorm

A responsive registration form that tells users when the inputs are incorrect

---

## Features

- **Real-time validation** Users see in real time if their input is wrong
- **Submit Double Check** Submit button double checks if the form is correct
- **Local Storage Save** Previous users will have their data saved after a successful registration

---

## Reflection
- event.preventDefault() helped with the form submission by not allowing the website to automatically refresh, deleting all the data we would want saved
- HTML5 validation gives you built-in browser rules out of the box, while JavaScript lets you build custom logic and styled error messages—and using both gives you the security of native rules with the polish of a custom user interface.
- I used local storage to store the form data into a variable then show on the username input field the previous username that was inputted previously. For sensitive data, it can be easily access and would be a security risk
- Well i mostly didn't know how it was supposed to be structured so I had to look up examples of how people usually structure these types of forms. Other than that lots of console.logging to see which conditions worked
- I used conditions to make sure the correct error messages were going to be processed.